BT 1 0 0 1 0 39 Tm 9.2 TL /F1 7 Tf .2 .254902 .333333 rg (In clinical diagnostic screening for Coronary Artery Disease, misclassification errors are inherently asymmetric. A ) Tj /F2 7 Tf (False Positive \(FP\)) Tj /F1 7 Tf ( misclassifies a healthy patient as) Tj T* -0.051444 Tw (diseased, resulting in emotional distress and confirmatory non-invasive testing \(e.g., stress echocardiography, coronary CT angiography\). Conversely, a ) Tj /F2 7 Tf (False Negative) Tj T* 0 Tw (\(FN\)) Tj /F1 7 Tf ( discharges a patient with active, obstructive coronary artery disease, denying them antiplatelet therapy, statins, or revascularization. This introduces an) Tj T* -0.076212 Tw (unacceptable risk of acute myocardial infarction or sudden cardiac death. Mathematically, the clinical loss function is: ) Tj /F2 7 Tf (L\(y, y) Tj /F5 7 Tf 9.2 TL (n) Tj /F2 7 Tf 9.2 TL (\) = C_FP \267 \(1 - y\) \267 y) Tj /F5 7 Tf 9.2 TL (n) Tj /F2 7 Tf 9.2 TL ( + C_FN \267 y \267 \(1 - y) Tj /F5 7 Tf 9.2 TL (n) Tj /F2 7 Tf 9.2 TL (\)) Tj /F1 7 Tf (,) Tj T* 0 Tw (where ) Tj /F2 7 Tf (C_FN / C_FP ) Tj /F6 7 Tf 9.2 TL (\273) Tj /F2 7 Tf 9.2 TL ( 5:1 to 10:1) Tj /F1 7 Tf (. Consequently, sensitivity / recall and ROC-AUC are established as the primary optimization metrics over raw accuracy.) Tj T* ET
